{"availability":"available","full":"sagezaugg/kh-tracker","name":"kh-tracker","description":"Unofficial 100% completion tracker for Kingdom Hearts Final Mix and Kingdom Hearts II Final Mix, with PC save import. Fan project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-08T19:56:47Z","updated":"2026-10-08T23:34:17Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kh-tracker.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://kh-tracker.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:14.909Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:14.909Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:14.909Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:14.909Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An unofficial, fan-made 100% completion tracker for Kingdom Hearts Final Mix and Kingdom Hearts II Final Mix, with save-file import. It's a single-page app (Vite + React 18 + TypeScript, React Router v6, Zustand) styled after the KH2 pause menu. One site, with a game switcher in the header.","Each game tracks three definitions of 100% from one checklist: Jiminy's Journal, Trophies (Platinum excluded from the count) and Everything. Importing a PC save fills in most of the checklist; the file never leaves the browser. In Chrome and Edge the tracker can also watch the save file and re-import it every time the game saves (Config, Auto re-import).","There's also a save diff tool at /tools/save-diff: load a save from before and after an in-game event to see every byte and bit that changed. It's how the remaining unknown flags get mapped."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sagezaugg/kh-tracker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"dbfa67fc6a46ff131bc13ca559a24adcef48116c257a1a709b5a1aa77d093f64","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:15.058Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:15.058Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An unofficial, fan-made 100% completion tracker for Kingdo